#' Mgat3 mouse brain and kidney N-glycan source profiles
#'
#' Source-preserving study-level N-glycan resource from Mgat3 wild-type and
#' knockout mouse brain and kidney. It contains the complete published
#' 51-feature brain table and 287-feature kidney workbook as distinct source
#' panels.
#'
#' @details
#' The object is a disjoint union of 338 source-specific chromatographic
#' features across six source observations: two genotype-labelled brain
#' profiles and four kidney sample/run columns. Of the 2,028 storage cells,
#' 1,250 are measured source cells and 778 cross-panel combinations are
#' unmeasured; source_coverage and processing_masks distinguish these from the
#' 324 source zeros represented as NA. The original brain and kidney matrices,
#' annotations, sample metadata and exact maps remain in metadata(x)$panels,
#' panel_row_data, panel_col_data and panel_maps. No rows are aligned across
#' tissues using composition, mass or author numbering.
#'
#' The one abundance assay retains EIC peak intensities in panel-specific
#' instrument units. Brain uses aminoxyTMT6 whereas kidney uses aminoxyTMT0;
#' combining storage does not establish calibrated numerical comparability
#' across tissues or protocols. Original percentages remain
#' metadata(x)$source_relative_abundance, not a second assay. Both source
#' percentage blocks use high-mannose intensity sums as denominators rather
#' than total glycome. Brain values retain the published one-decimal
#' precision; kidney values retain Excel precision. No averaging, imputation
#' or normalization is added.
#'
#' Kidney workbook run IDs exactly match four GPST000031 raw filenames. Brain
#' S2C supplies no run or replicate IDs; its raw-file links are explicitly
#' marked genotype-and-filename-based candidates in GPST000027. Although the
#' article reports three independent brain WT/KO pairs, only two genotype
#' columns are published in S2C; these are not expanded or labelled as
#' independent individual mice. Biological replication, pairing, age and sex
#' are not inferred. This object represents the complete published tables, not
#' every raw detected peak or every experiment in the paper.
#'
#' 306 features have a single source composition, retaining generic residues
#' plus the explicitly stated Man3GlcNAc2 core. For 32 ambiguous kidney
#' features, typed composition is NA while every original candidate
#' string/count and all quantitative cells remain. Chromatographic subpeaks
#' stay distinct even when composition and mass match. Diagnostic MS/MS scan
#' identifiers do not establish complete topology; no glycan_structure column
#' is present. Source file attribution and article-version CC BY 4.0 license
#' evidence are retained separately from the package code license; no
#' supplement-specific license declaration was independently verified.
#'
#' @format
#' A [glyexp::GlycomicSE] with 338 features and 6 observations. The abundance
#' assay is in source EIC peak intensity (panel-specific instrument units).
#' rowData has no glycan_structure column because no feature has a supported
#' structural annotation.
#' @source
#' GlycoPOST GPST000027 and GPST000031. Supplementary Figure S2C (PDF page 4)
#' and Supplemental Table S2 (WT&Mgat3KO sheet). Study:
#' \url{https://doi.org/10.1074/mcp.RA119.001534}. Repository:
#' \url{https://glycopost.glycosmos.org/entry/GPST000027} and
#' \url{https://glycopost.glycosmos.org/entry/GPST000031}. Quantitative
#' source: \url{https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6773561/}.
#' @seealso [glyhub_data_conventions] for missing-value handling, annotations
#'   and access to original measurements and source coordinates.
#' @keywords datasets
#' @name glyhub_GPST000027_031_N
#' @section Access:
#' Use `glyhub_load("glyhub_GPST000027_031_N")` to load this dataset.
#' @inheritParams glyhub_load
#' @export
